# Summary
Introduced a privacy/security bug: the auto-capture-specific Discord enabled flag no longer gates auto-capture uploads. The upload path is now enabled by the unrelated global output.uploadDiscord setting and can use a disabled auto-capture webhook URL.
The new autoCaptureDiscordUploadEnabled helper returns true when either autoCapture.discord.enabled or the global output.uploadDiscord flag is set. finalizeAutoCaptureImage then uploads every auto-capture result and first prefers autoCapture.discord.webhookUrl before falling back to the primary Discord webhook. This means an existing or imported configuration with autoCapture.schedule.enabled=true, output.uploadDiscord=true, and autoCapture.discord.enabled=false will start posting scheduled/test auto-capture images after this update. If a stale or attacker-supplied autoCapture.discord.webhookUrl is present, it is used even though the auto-capture Discord feature is disabled. This can disclose VRChat capture images and configured Discord presence metadata to an unintended Discord webhook. Webhook URL validation still restricts the destination to Discord, so this is an information disclosure/consent bypass rather than arbitrary SSRF or code execution.

